# FreeField Settings — env template (Wave 18, spec §8)
# Copy values into .env.local (dev) or your deploy environment.
# NEVER commit real secret values. SecretRef placeholders only.

# --- Channel A: Sentry (three-channel telemetry, wave 18) ---
# DSN for the ff-field-web project (environments: production/development).
# Absent => initTelemetry keeps the documented no-op local-only v1 path.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=<sentry-dsn:secretref/ff/telemetry>
# Release identity at build time (CI/deploy sets to the git sha). Optional.
VITE_SENTRY_RELEASE=<git-sha:provided-by-deploy>
# Sentry auth token + org/project slugs live in CI/deploy env ONLY
# (never in any committed .env*). The vite plugin skips sourcemap
# upload when they are absent — see apps/settings/vite.config.ts gate.
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=<ci-only>
# SENTRY_ORG=<ci-only>
# SENTRY_PROJECT=ff-field-web

# --- Channel C: Firebase Analytics rollups (spec §5.6) ---
# Remote Config key `telemetry_sampling_pct` (0–100, default 0 until
# prod RC ships; fetch failure => fail-CLOSED 0%). Per-user opt-in is
# stored client-side (key `ff.analytics.optIn`); UI toggle ships in a
# later wave. Crash channels A+B are always on and PII-free by scrub.

# --- Existing Firebase client config (unchanged) ---
# VITE_FIREBASE_* keys keep their current values in .env.local /
# .env.production; they are not part of wave 18.
